    "en":  {
               "headline":  "Record revenue, but margin and loss worries push ONDS to a 52-week low",
               "technical":  "The trend is clearly down. On 20 Nov 2026 ONDS closed at $3.76, down 11.11% on the day. That is far below the EMA 50 ($6.15), EMA 100 ($7.02) and EMA 200 ($7.54). EMAs are smoothed average prices over 50, 100 and 200 days. They are stacked in bearish order, with the shortest below the longest, which marks a well-established downtrend. Momentum is still falling. MACD (a trend-momentum gauge) is -0.63, below its signal line at -0.50, and the histogram is negative at -0.13. RSI 14 is 28.68. RSI is a 0–100 momentum gauge where under 30 counts as oversold, so selling is stretched and short bounces become more likely. Price sits just above the lower Bollinger Band at $3.69. Bollinger Bands mark a typical 20-day trading range, and its middle line is $5.44. The day\u0027s low of $3.73 is also the 52-week low, about 75% below the 52-week high of $15.28. Volume was 47.5M shares, only about 2% above the 20-day average of 46.5M. That is not the heavy volume that usually marks a selling climax. Nearby support is $3.69–3.73, and the first resistance is around $5.44.",
               "fundamental":  "Ondas is now mostly a defense and autonomy company assembled through acquisitions. Q3 2026 results came out on 12 Nov. Revenue was $167.5M, double Q2\u0027s $83.8M and above the roughly $148M consensus. Backlog rose 36% from Q2 to $835M. GAAP gross margin fell to 21.8% from 43.1% in Q2. Management blamed production inefficiencies in precision-strike programs and accounting charges tied to acquisitions. The adjusted EBITDA loss widened to $59.7M, worse than the roughly $40M consensus. Guidance went up: Q4 revenue above $250M, FY2026 at least $550M and FY2027 at least $1.1B, excluding further acquisitions. Company-wide EBITDA breakeven is now targeted for Q3 2027. Cash and investments of $820M give it room to keep operating. For the moat, demand is real, but profitable delivery at scale is not yet proven.",
               "news":  [
                            "12 Nov 2026: Q3 revenue was a record $167.5M with $214M of new orders. Ondas raised its FY2026 revenue target to at least $550M and set a 2027 target of at least $1.1B. Shares still fell because of the margin collapse and the larger EBITDA loss.",
                            "13–16 Nov 2026: Needham and Lake Street cut their price targets from $19 to $14, Northland from $18 to $13, Maxim from $22 to $18 and Stifel from $18 to $15. All kept Buy ratings and cited the EBITDA miss and lower valuations across peer companies.",
                            "5 Nov 2026: Ondas agreed to buy Stemme GmbH, the German maker of the airframe used in its ULTRA long-endurance surveillance aircraft, in an all-cash deal with no price disclosed. The goal is 10 ULTRA aircraft a month by 2028, and closing is expected in Q1 2027. The stock fell about 9% to $5.27 that day.",
                            "Q3 operations: Ondas won $100M in Sentinel bookings, including $53.7M of ULTRA follow-on orders, and a U.S. Army follow-on task order. Its Sentrycs counter-drone systems were deployed at 2026 FIFA World Cup and NFL stadiums.",
                            "20 Nov 2026: The stock fell 11.11% to a new 52-week low of $3.73 intraday. No new company announcement explains it. Small insider sales by two directors and the COO were disclosed the same day, each about $20K at an average of $4.08."
                        ],
               "caution":  "The main risk is that growth is coming through acquisitions and is burning cash. Gross margin halved in one quarter, and the EBITDA loss is getting bigger as revenue rises. The Q4 2026 target to turn the core operating businesses EBITDA-positive is the next credibility test. The January 2026 share offering also came with 121.6M warrants at a $28 exercise price, which leaves a large overhang of potential new shares. Momentum indicators are still falling, and volume shows no sign that selling has run its course. An oversold RSI can stay oversold for weeks.",
               "opportunity":  "The business numbers keep improving even as the stock falls. The $835M backlog is about 1.5 times the FY2026 revenue target, guidance was raised and the 2027 target is about double this year\u0027s. Every analyst who cut a price target kept a Buy rating. RSI under 30 and price at the lower Bollinger Band show selling is stretched. If gross margin recovers to the mid-30s as guided and Q4 revenue comes in above $250M, the market\u0027s view of the stock could change quickly.",
               "risks":  [
                             "Gross margin could stay low if precision-strike production problems persist",
                             "The company-wide EBITDA breakeven target of Q3 2027 could slip",
                             "Dilution from outstanding warrants and from paying for acquisitions with stock",
                             "Risk of combining many acquired companies in a short time",
                             "Lower valuations for defense-tech peers and U.S. budget uncertainty after the midterms",
                             "Technical downtrend with no confirmed bottom"
                         ],
               "summary":  "ONDS is in a strong technical downtrend. Price is below all three EMAs, MACD is negative and the stock is at its 52-week low, though RSI 28.68 shows it is oversold. The drop since 12 Nov reflects worries about profitability, not demand. Revenue doubled from Q2, backlog reached $835M and guidance went up, but gross margin halved and losses widened. The early-commercial-autonomy thesis is not broken, but it is on watch. The next checks are Q4 margins and whether the core businesses turn EBITDA-positive."
